# Trivy ignore file, applied to every filesystem and image scan in CI and pre-commit.
#
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line, optionally with an expiry date after which the
# entry stops applying and the finding blocks the build again:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# Every entry must say why it is accepted. Review the list when an entry expires or when
# the base image changes.

# perl-base in the Debian 13 layer of python:3.14-slim. Debian has marked these as
# affected with no fix available, or fix deferred. perl-base is an Essential package and
# cannot be removed from the image; nothing in CredShare executes Perl, so the code paths
# are unreachable at runtime. Re-check with `trivy image python:3.14-slim` before renewing.
CVE-2026-13221 exp:2026-12-04
CVE-2026-42496 exp:2026-12-04
CVE-2026-8376 exp:2026-12-04
